---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import {SITE} from '../site';

const title = 'Privacy Policy: a Local-Only Tab Manager | TabLodge';
const description =
	'TabLodge keeps your tab sessions and bookmarks on your device. No accounts, no servers, no analytics, no network requests. Read what it stores and why each permission is needed.';

const permissions = [
	['tabs', 'Reading tab URLs, titles and placement to save sessions; opening tabs to restore them.'],
	['tabGroups', 'Saving and recreating native tab groups.'],
	['bookmarks', 'Importing your browser bookmarks when you ask, and noticing a page you bookmark in the browser if you turn on that setting (off by default).'],
	['favicon', 'Showing site icons from the browser\'s local cache.'],
	['storage, unlimitedStorage', 'Keeping your data in local extension storage without the default size cap.'],
	['contextMenus', 'Optional right-click save and bookmark actions.'],
	['clipboardWrite', 'Copying bookmark URLs and session links when you ask.'],
	['sidePanel', 'Showing bookmarks, sessions and open tabs in the browser side panel.'],
	['search', 'Running a web search with your default engine, only when you choose "Search the web".'],
	['alarms', 'Scheduling crash-recovery snapshots, automatic backups and trash bin cleanup.'],
	['downloads (optional)', 'Saving backup copies to your Downloads folder, only if you turn that on; turning it off gives the permission back.'],
];
---

<Base
	title={title}
	description={description}
	path="/privacy/"
	breadcrumbs={[
		{name: 'Home', path: '/'},
		{name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/'},
	]}
	jsonLd={[
		{
			'@type': 'WebPage',
			'@id': 'https://tablodge.bbay.dev/privacy/#webpage',
			url: 'https://tablodge.bbay.dev/privacy/',
			name: title,
			description,
			dateModified: '2026-10-25',
			isPartOf: {'@id': 'https://tablodge.bbay.dev/#website'},
		},
	]}
>
	<article class="narrow prose page">
		<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <span aria-current="page">Privacy</span></nav>
		<h1>Privacy</h1>
		<p class="note">Last updated: 2026-10-26</p>
		<p class="lead">
			TabLodge keeps your sessions, bookmarks and settings in your browser profile. It has no accounts or backend, and <strong>does not collect or upload your data.</strong>
		</p>

		<h2>What TabLodge does not do</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>No accounts, servers or cloud sync. TabLodge has no backend.</li>
			<li>No analytics, telemetry, crash reporting or advertising.</li>
			<li>No network requests of its own. All code, styles, fonts and icons are bundled in the extension; nothing is loaded from a CDN.</li>
			<li>No website access. TabLodge requests no host permissions, injects no content scripts and never reads page contents.</li>
			<li>No sale or sharing of data with anyone.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>What TabLodge stores, and where</h2>
		<p>Everything is stored locally in your browser profile:</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Extension storage</strong> (<code>chrome.storage.local</code>, key <code>tablodge.state</code>): your saved sessions (tab titles, URLs, notes, pinned, tab-group and split-view info), folders, bookmark columns and bookmarks, settings, and excluded websites.</li>
			<li><strong>Extension storage</strong> (<code>uiTheme</code>) and the extension's <code>localStorage</code> (<code>tablodge.uiTheme</code>): your Light, Dark or System appearance choice, and a copy used to paint each page in the right theme before it loads.</li>
			<li><strong>Recovery data</strong> (extension storage): rolling snapshots of your open windows for crash recovery, automatic and safety backups, the trash bin, and short-lived Undo copies (kept for two minutes). Snapshots skip private windows and excluded websites.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			TabLodge reads tab details to save and restore sessions, find duplicates, show and search open tabs, and capture recovery snapshots. Snapshots are enabled by default and can be turned off in Settings, under Recovery &amp; backups. It reads your browser's bookmark tree only when you ask to import it. If you enable the browser bookmark setting, it also watches for newly created bookmarks to offer to add that page or add it automatically. That setting is off by default. Site icons come from the browser's local favicon cache.
		</p>
		<p>
			Saved sessions and bookmarks stay until you delete them. Trash is kept for 7, 30 or 90 days, depending on your setting. Snapshots, backups and Undo copies also have retention or size limits. You can clear recovery data in <strong>Settings &rsaquo; Recovery &amp; backups</strong>. Erasing sessions or bookmarks in <strong>Settings &rsaquo; Data</strong> creates a safety backup, so check the backup history too if you want to remove retained copies. Removing the extension deletes its browser storage.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you enable backup copies in Downloads, TabLodge writes JSON files to <code>Downloads/TabLodge/</code>. Turning the setting off or uninstalling does not delete those files. Exports, including JSON, HTML, CSV, Markdown, URL lists and full backup ZIP files, are not encrypted. Keep them private if their titles, URLs or notes are sensitive. A folder synced by another app may upload them.
		</p>
		<p>
			Opening a saved link loads that website normally. An optional setting, off by default, removes common tracking parameters from the destination when opening saved links or restoring sessions and snapshots. It leaves the URLs in your library unchanged. Choosing <strong>Search the web</strong> sends your query to the browser's default search engine. These are actions you request, not background reporting by TabLodge.
		</p>

		<h2>Permissions</h2>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Permission</th><th scope="col">Used for</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>
					{permissions.map(([name, use]) => <tr><th scope="row"><code>{name}</code></th><td>{use}</td></tr>)}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>

		<h2>This website</h2>
		<p>
			This site (tablodge.bbay.dev) is a static page with no analytics, cookies or third-party scripts. It is hosted on GitHub Pages, which, like any web host, may keep ordinary server logs; see <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>. Manual release downloads are served by GitHub Releases. Chrome Web Store listings, installations, and updates are handled by Google through the <a href={SITE.chromeWebStore} rel="noopener">store</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>Questions or concerns: <a href={SITE.issues} rel="noopener">open an issue on GitHub</a>.</p>
	</article>
</Base>

<style>
	.page {
		padding-block: 3rem 5rem;
	}
	.crumbs {
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
</style>
